From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/gem: bound dma_resv and dma_fence waits in close/release paths

msm_gem_close() and msm_gem_dmabuf_release() call dma_resv_wait_timeout()
with MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT and interruptible=false, and msm_gem_vm_close()
calls dma_fence_wait() with intr=false.

When a process (such as gamescope, mangoapp, or sway) exits or closes a
GEM handle / dmabuf fd while a GPU fence on that buffer object is wedged
behind a failing GMU resume or GPU recovery worker, the thread enters an
unbounded TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE (D-state) sleep waiting on the reservation
or VM fence, blocking process teardown and session restart indefinitely.

Bound these three teardown waits to 2000 ms (msecs_to_jiffies(2000)),
matching the 2-second timeout used elsewhere in drm/msm recovery paths, so
that handle, dmabuf, and VM teardown can proceed even if the GPU/GMU is
wedged.

Signed-off-by: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c       | 2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_prime.c | 2 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c   | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@
 	 * in CLOSE ioctl
 	 */
 	dma_resv_wait_timeout(obj->resv, DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP, false,
-			      MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT);
+			      msecs_to_jiffies(2000));
 
 	/*
 	 * Merge the KMS-VM teardown (if vma_ref hits 0) with the user-VM
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_prime.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_prime.c
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 	struct drm_gem_object *obj = dma_buf->priv;
 
 	dma_resv_wait_timeout(obj->resv, DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP, false,
-			      MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT);
+			      msecs_to_jiffies(2000));
 
 	msm_gem_vma_put(obj);
 	drm_gem_dmabuf_release(dma_buf);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
@@ -915,7 +915,7 @@
 		return;
 
 	if (vm->last_fence)
-		dma_fence_wait(vm->last_fence, false);
+		dma_fence_wait_timeout(vm->last_fence, false, msecs_to_jiffies(2000));
 
 	/* Kill the scheduler now, so we aren't racing with it for cleanup: */
 	drm_sched_stop(&vm->sched, NULL);
